 r"I am writing to apply for the Graduate -- Digital -- Data, AI \& Engineering programme at bp in the UK. I completed an MSc in Health Data Science at University College London in September 2026, where a distinction is expected, after a BSc in Biological Sciences at Imperial College London, and I currently work as a Data Analyst Intern at TikTok Shop UK. Across my academic and professional experience I have built data pipelines, machine learning models and AI applications, and turned them into tools that people use to make decisions.",

 r"What attracts me most to bp is that the work has a visible end point: energy delivered at scale to millions of customers today, while the business invests in the energy transition. The programme's three rotations across data science, machine learning engineering, AI engineering and analytics are exactly how I would like to grow, by building real data products and AI-enabled applications before choosing where to go deeper. I enjoy taking an unclear business problem, understanding what the people who own it actually need, and turning it into a solution that can be tested and improved.",

 r"At TikTok Shop UK I analyse merchant and transaction data in SQL and Python and build the KPI frameworks and dashboards that operations, product and commercial teams use to set targets and track initiatives. When my supervisor asked me to configure a merchant campaign by hand, I worked out the logic and used Claude Code to build an AI agent with a validation step to check its accuracy. It cut the time the task took by around 40 to 50 percent, and it taught me that automation is only valuable when people can trust its output.",

 r"At DS Digital Technology I worked as a Data Scientist Intern on a patient-facing AI product for a pharmaceutical client. I built a Python pipeline that called six LLM APIs with retrieval augmentation and scored more than 2,400 responses against a 246-question benchmark that the client adopted as its acceptance standard, and I designed blinded A/B tests to check whether a new knowledge-graph feature genuinely improved the answers. I learned to define what success looks like with the subject matter experts before writing any code.",

 r"My MSc dissertation applied machine learning to 458,840 UK Biobank participants, comparing logistic regression with three tree ensembles and using causal forests to estimate the effect of lifestyle change, and I delivered the results as an interactive Streamlit app for non-specialists. Earlier, at Westlake University, I refactored and parallelised a research pipeline in Python and R, cutting processing time by around 60 percent, and moved it into version-controlled scripts so that others could reproduce it.",

 r"I would bring bp strong Python and SQL, hands-on experience across machine learning, LLM applications and data pipelines, and the ability to explain technical findings clearly to non-technical colleagues. I have the right to work in the UK until January 2029, and I am based in London and happy to work from any of the programme's offices.",

 r"Thank you for considering my application. I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my experience in data science, AI and automation could contribute to bp's digital graduate programme.",
